3 656 Q 1376 384 1805 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-30\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(58.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-18\" transform=\"translate(93.1875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5\" transform=\"translate(149.984375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" transform=\"translate(207.984375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" transform=\"translate(262.890625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(319.6875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(354.78125 0)\"/></g></g></g><g id=\"patch_3\"><path d=\"M 67.225455 133.76 L 207.007273 133.76 L 207.007273 17.6 L 67.225455 17.6 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p3592f17597)\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 241.952727 133.76 L 381.734545 133.76 L 381.734545 93.9752 L 241.952727 93.9752 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p3592f17597)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 51.5 133.76 L 51.5 11.792 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 51.5 133.76 L 397.46 133.76 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(126.428239 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-5d\" d=\"M 870 749 Q 1075 749 1168 643 Q 1261 538 1261 371 L 1261 282 Q 1261 26 1107 -294 Q 954 -614 678 -851 L 250 -851 Q 442 -646 560 -464 Q 678 -282 730 -58 Q 602 -26 541 64 Q 480 154 480 282 L 480 371 Q 480 538 576 643 Q 672 749 870 749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5d\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(207.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(304.643636 91.7752) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" d=\"M 2912 0 L 2400 0 L 2400 877 L 243 877 L 243 1350 L 2112 4467 L 2912 4467 L 2912 1325 L 3558 1325 L 3558 877 L 2912 877 L 2912 0 z\nM 2368 4051 L 749 1325 L 2400 1325 L 2400 4051 L 2368 4051 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p3592f17597\"><rect x=\"51.5\" y=\"11.792\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Extra students reaching the reading standard","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Tutoring:</b> $4.8M ÷ $1,200 = 4,000 students tutored (all of them below standard; there are 4,000), of whom about <b>1,200</b> reach the standard.</p> <p><b>Smaller classes:</b> $4.8M ÷ $700 = 6,857 students covered; about <b>411</b> more reach the standard.</p>"},{"q":"Teachers argue smaller classes help every child, not just those behind. How do you respond?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>They're right that smaller classes have wider benefits, like behaviour and teacher workload, that this measure doesn't capture. But this grant's goal is reading results, and tutoring delivers far more of them. Involve teachers: let them choose which students are tutored and align tutoring with classroom lessons. Revisit class sizes if longer-term funding comes.</p>"}],"reco":"Fund small-group tutoring. It costs about $4,000 per extra student reaching the reading standard, against about $11,700 for smaller classes, so the $4.8M would bring about 1,200 students up to standard rather than about 411. Tutoring also targets the students who are behind and can start within a term, while extra classrooms aren't available everywhere. Involve teachers in choosing students and linking tutoring to lessons. Risk: tutor quality, so train and monitor them. Next step: recruit tutors and test students at the start and end of the year.","great":["Defines the outcome precisely","Computes cost per outcome for both plans","Notes that one plan targets the students in need","Engages the teachers' argument rather than dismissing it"],"id":94,"slug":"lakeside-school-district"}